  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "As the disc is in combined rotation and translation, each point has a tangential velocity and a linear velocity in the forward direction. From figure $\\mathrm{v}_{\\text {net }}$ (for lowest point) $=\\mathrm{v}-\\mathrm{R} \\omega=\\mathrm{v}-\\mathrm{v}=0$\r\n\r\nand acceleration\r\n\r\n$=\\frac{\\mathrm{v}^{2}}{\\mathrm{R}}+0=\\frac{\\mathrm{v}^{2}}{\\mathrm{R}}$\r\n\r\n<img src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/pyq/bitsat/EyZu6lGUGQJRjAdr1OzjBi45khqyYV8BsmqTxCDUKjw.original.fullsize.png\"><br>\r\n\r\n(since linear speed is constant)",
    "image": null
